{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501547-ways-for-preventing-and-or-cancelling-blood-bonds","id":1501547,"title":"Ways for preventing and/or cancelling blood bonds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-28T11:17:46-08:00","id":1501547,"title":"Ways for preventing and/or cancelling blood bonds","content":"...with minimal fuss, either permanently or repeatedly. In particular, I'd like ways to give the effects of the &quot;unbondable&quot; merit or to &quot;neutralise&quot; a vampire's vitae. Preferably at a price. I'm kind of bouncing ideas around, trying to find something that's not too far out of the bounds of canon/RAW/whatever. It might be something I build a story around.<br /> <br /> Obviously, there's blood sorcery. There are a handful of painful sounding rituals, so options for that would be &quot;be a Tremere,&quot; the rather ominous &quot;suck it up and give a Tremere leverage over you so they'll use the horrible painful rituals on you... repeatedly,&quot; or &quot;somehow get a sorcerer to agree to teach you this so you can do it yourself.&quot; There's no Akhu rituals that I know of, but with their religion's thing for breaking, making and manipulating chains, Setite Lector Priests might be able to break bonds if you're willing to get into debt with them, perhaps?<br /> <br /> You can try to get the secrets to the Vaulderie from the Sabbat somehow. The vinculum is barely any better than the bond, the Sabbat absolutely will not be willing to teach you and the Camarilla is going to be very interested in finding out where the fuck you got your hands on that knowledge, potential Sabbat infiltrator. This is a terrible option, but technically an option.<br /> <br /> I imagine making a deal with demons could make something work, if you're a moron who doesn't mind gaining immunity to slavery A through signing on for slavery B.<br /> <br /> I think cross-splat deals might be possible?<br /> <br /> Mages can do just about anything, assuming they're willing to help you and you don't mind putting up with owing them a favour and getting potentially dragged into Awakened bullshit and potential paradox side-effects.<br /> <br /> The Lifeweb arcanos technically affects the connection between Wraiths and their fetters but under the tradition of &quot;I'm the storyteller, things work how I say they do&quot; and some vague overlap between the dead and undead, maybe it could affect blood bonds?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T11:30:58-08:00","id":1501551,"title":"","content":"The specific parameters of how something like this would work would probably be dependent on the sort of story you want to tell and chronicle you want to run. By RAW my take on the Blood Bond is that it\u2019s meant to be an incredibly horrifying thing which is part-and-parcel with the perverted nature of vampiric existence, where the only certain* means of ensuring loyalty amongst your own kind is blood slavery in the form of quasi-devotion and that breaking that is difficult or costly.<br /> <br /> I do agree with you that the main vampiric notions that come to mind for me are Blood Sorcery (which would likely involve heavy debt to the Tremere, Settites, or whoever you get to pull it off), the Sabbat (who do offer relative freedom but on the terms of joining their ranks), or Infernalism (which is as dubious as you mention).<br /> <br /> As far as cross-splats go:<br /> <br /> I think that most methods the Changing Breeds could bring to bear would have undesirable side effects (Yes, being immersed in the great silver lake of purification in the umbra realms will dissolve the blood bond, but it will also dissolve your entire cursed existence as you are utterly unclean). Aside from that, if such a plot line interests you, I could hypothetically see the Changing Breed priests attaching you to a powerful spirit who could forestall the bond in exchange for service to them instead.<br /> <br /> The Awakened are another option of course, although this gets into the classic crossover questions that come along with Mages. Can the Awakened do anything with enough Arete or do they need to roll more successes then G-d? It\u2019s hard to say. I\u2019m inclined to say that a Mage who cared to investigate the matter could definitely provide leads into how the vampire might be able to slip their metaphysical bonds but I\u2019d be wary of letting Mages be able to completely remove them.<br /> <br /> Wraiths and Changelings might be able to help by spiriting the vampire off into their respective dimensions, away from their domitors, but that of course carries its own issues.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it depends most on what sort of genre and theme you want for your chronicle. How you view the Blood Bond as a narrative element and thematic object should help to highlight the spectrum of possibilities available for you within the narrative.<br /> <br /> I hope this was helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T22:27:20-08:00","id":1501587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501547-ways-for-preventing-and-or-cancelling-blood-bonds?p=1501551#post1501551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Awakened are another option of course, although this gets into the classic crossover questions that come along with Mages. Can the Awakened do anything with enough Arete or do they need to roll more successes then G-d? It\u2019s hard to say. I\u2019m inclined to say that a Mage who cared to investigate the matter could definitely provide leads into how the vampire might be able to slip their metaphysical bonds but I\u2019d be wary of letting Mages be able to completely remove them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. For one, I don't think you're really rolling more successes than G-d, because that's in reference to the curse of vampirism in general, not a Blood Bond. Two separate metaphysical matters.<br /> <br /> Second, I'm generally of the opinion that a Mage could theoretically do anything, with the right Spheres. This doesn't mean it's not <i>difficult</i>.<br /> <br /> I would imagine if a Mage could, it would require a great deal of dedicated research, testing, and rare materials. <s>A Rote to break a Blood Bond has probably never been developed, or if it has it's lost knowledge.</s> (For a certain value of &quot;lost&quot;, of course. You could make a whole Chronicle about tracking down some ancient tome or stone tablet collecting a bygone Mage's notes on how to sever vampiric bonds).<br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, we're assuming we're talking about a Mage severing a Blood Bond on behalf of a vampire. It's WAY more likely that a Mage, at some point in history, figured out a Rote for breaking Blood Bonds in general. Because there's probably been many times a Mage has been motivated to save a mortal from their vampire Regnant. Hell, multiple Traditions/Conventions/Crafts probably have that on file, just in case.<br /> <br /> Whether they'll let you see it if they know you're trying to free a <i>vampire</i> is another matter.<br /> <br /> So, you know, just don't tell them. Easy, right? /s<br /> <br /> Point is, I don't think it should be especially difficult for a Mage to accomplish the task of breaking Blood Bonds. The difficulty should be in convincing a Mage to do it, and in repaying the debt. The ST can make that as easy or as hard as they like, for Chronicle purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-29-2023, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T08:17:22-08:00","id":1501616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501547-ways-for-preventing-and-or-cancelling-blood-bonds?p=1501551#post1501551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as cross-splats go:<br /> <br /> I think that most methods the Changing Breeds could bring to bear would have undesirable side effects (Yes, being immersed in the great silver lake of purification in the umbra realms will dissolve the blood bond, but it will also dissolve your entire cursed existence as you are utterly unclean). Aside from that, if such a plot line interests you, I could hypothetically see the Changing Breed priests attaching you to a powerful spirit who could forestall the bond in exchange for service to them instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erebus doesn't kill. That's the big thing about it - you'll suffer for as long as you hold onto the tainted bits of yourself, but as soon as they're gone, you'll be cleansed and you can leave physically and spiritually whole. But that's far from the only way; Shadow Lords of the Bringers of Light camp found out how to break the blood bond, though it's a rather high ranked Gift taught by an avatar of Grandfather Thunder. There are probably other spirits that can provide a similar effect, though finding it out past the veil of secrecy that they keep might be the biggest hurdle. I believe that Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion might also be able to burn it out with sunfire, but that's exchanging the time you spend in Erebus for way more immediate pain and potential harm/death, and comes way closer to the impression that you had of Erebus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T17:13:05-08:00","id":1501651,"title":"","content":"You know, Erebus would probably cure of Vampirism if you managed to get through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}